      "body": "## Purpose\n\nContinue W7 from the completed W6 guarded-agreement qualification, integrating current main and preserving a consumer for the exact installed Linux package prepared in CrispEmbed PR #237.\n\n**Current status: paired package controls/build/install passed. The new Dart consumer is saved source-only and remains uncompiled because the workspace filled before commands could start. This PR remains draft.**\n\nThis PR is stacked on `feat/native-spacy-reference-20261117` / PR #139 so the W7 changes remain reviewable separately from the completed W6 work.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Merge main `482e0817` at `13747281`, retaining its 72 evidence files. No production source changes; all 342 sealed source blob identities still match the original candidate.\n- Preserve the complete source-refresh inventory, original native/model restoration evidence, package build/install receipts and frozen operational protocol.\n- Add `packages/quds_proofing_spacy/tool/consume_distribution.dart` as a source-only developer consumer. It is intended to authenticate the installed package and runtime, exercise the actual owned Quds worker, verify original coordinates and copied annotations, and observe explicit locale, caller-cancellation, disposal and reopen behavior.\n- Check the actual existing Quds APIs and distribution/protocol schemas; use typed checked JSON readers and explicit annotation comparisons. Static review is recorded separately from execution.\n- Correct the stale package notice and save exact checkpoints, evidence limitations and instructions for resuming in a workspace with capacity.\n\n## Observed validation and pending gates\n\nThe paired packager's 25 model-free controls, real package build and immutable installation passed. Native/model restoration matched the 15 native files, 5 model files and all 6 recorded system dependencies.\n\nAn authenticated minimal Dart 3.13.7 VM and three pinned packages successfully imported the existing native package, hashed `abc` and allocated an FFI Arena before later ENOSPC. That probe did not compile the new driver. The full raw SDK/review receipts could not be reread after ENOSPC; the checkpoint retains only the previously observed metadata and hashes.\n\nPending: compile/run the current driver's `--self-test`, save the checked source and outcomes, then execute the installed-package worker consumer with a fresh report and external timeout. The corrected paired Python consumer's current 21 controls and first operational run are also pending. No claim of Flutter UI observation, physical native-compute interruption, mobile coverage or broad Linux portability is made.\n\n## Boundaries and recovery\n\nThe accepted native/model bytes, consumed native acceptance and W6 grammar results are preserved. The manual provider stays disabled by default, with no automatic Studio registration. Hosted artifact publication/download readback and production activation remain separate work.\n\nLocal sandbox startup reports `No space left on device`; even task-owned cleanup could not launch. Remote saves used non-forced expected-head updates and exact file/tree readback. No GitHub Actions query, wait, rerun or dispatch was performed.\n\n- [Saved continuation instructions](https://github.com/CrispStrobe/quds_office_suite/blob/225eeb921856b8728caf7254c91badf541d3e683/docs/validation/native-spacy-w7-20261118/CONTINUE.md)\n- [Exact completed/pending status](https://github.com/CrispStrobe/quds_office_suite/blob/225eeb921856b8728caf7254c91badf541d3e683/docs/validation/native-spacy-w7-20261118/checkpoint-status.json)\n- [Dart source-only checkpoint](https://github.com/CrispStrobe/quds_office_suite/blob/225eeb921856b8728caf7254c91badf541d3e683/docs/validation/native-spacy-w7-20261118/dart-consumer-checkpoint.json)\n- Paired CrispEmbed package: https://github.com/CrispStrobe/CrispEmbed/pull/237\n\nA subsequent read-only workspace probe also failed before the command ran, with an execution-service `No such file or directory` error. Current local mounting, contents and free space cannot be verified; the error does not establish file deletion. The remote source and handoff were independently read back and verified.\n",
